        "id": 1002971
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-31T18:07:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is a good point. A more targeted approach would be to issue one GetSubTreePaths call per known chassis path (e.g. /inventory/system/chassis1, /inventory/system/chassis2, …) and union the results, which would keep the scope tight. For now the single broad query is more simple, but we could switch to per-chassis queries if we want to keep the lookup cost bounded.",
      "parentUuid": "0d809a17_41d6b522",
      "revId": "3a5176f69a0f3a1042569b073e8db5b14bf372c4",
